exports[`generatePrompt > snapshot: link-initials 1`] = `
"# Add a "Made by" signature badge to this project

## Goal

Add this signature badge to the current project where the user wants it (in the footer if they haven't said where), using the project's own stack and conventions (components, styling approach, file structure). The badge reads "Crafted by Ada Lovelace".
Match the visual spec and behavior below exactly. The reference implementation at the end is the source of truth: adapt it to the project rather than pasting it as-is when a native approach fits better. Add no new dependency.

## Visual spec

- Layout: Pill. [avatar] · normal text · bold text · icon, in one row, vertically centered, no wrapping.
- Order: normal text, then bold text. One regular space between them.
- Normal text: "Crafted by", weight 400.
- Bold text: "Ada Lovelace", weight 500.
- Font: system stack only, no web font: -apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif.
- Size M: height 36px, font size 15px, padding 0 12px 0 4px, gap 8px.
- Corner radius: 18px (a full capsule).
- Border: none.
- Shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.08); on hover 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.12).
- Icon: an "arrow-up-right" (Lucide path: line 7,17 → 17,7 and polyline 7,7 17,7 17,17), 14px, 2px stroke, currentColor, in the icon color, aria-hidden (exact SVG in the reference).
- Avatar: round, 28px, background #FF6B35, initials "AL" in #000000, weight 600, 11px.
- Colors follow the site theme through prefers-color-scheme.
- Light palette:
  - Background: #FFFFFF
  - Border: #0000000D
  - Normal text: #6E6E73
  - Bold text: #000000
  - Icon: #6E6E73
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Dark palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Scope every class with a unique prefix and reset box-sizing, margin, padding, font, line-height and list-style on the badge and its children, so the host page CSS cannot leak in.

## Behavior

- Motion uses springs, expressed in CSS as linear() easings (values in the reference): fast = 0.08s, no bounce; moderate = 0.16s, no bounce; slow = 0.24s, bounce 0.12; slow exit = 0.16s tween. Never hard-code other durations.
- Mode: Link. The whole badge is one <a href="https://ada.dev"> opening in a new tab (target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer").
- Hover and keyboard focus: the arrow slides 2px up and 2px right (fast spring).
- Hover: the shadow grows as specified (fast spring).
- On appear: the badge gives a short horizontal shake (±3px). Animate a wrapper, not the clickable element, so the hover effect never restarts it.
- On delay: every 5s, starting 5s after load, the badge shows a sheen sweeping once from left to right across it (a gradient band on a clipped ::after: white on dark surfaces, a faint dark band on light ones). Loop it with CSS (one keyframe cycle per period), no timers.
- On hover: the badge scales to 1.04 (fast spring).
- prefers-reduced-motion: reduce → no movement, rotation or scaling; state changes are instant or fade only.

## Accessibility

- The link's accessible name is "Crafted by Ada Lovelace, opens in a new tab".
- Visible focus: a 2px outline in the bold text color, offset 2px, on :focus-visible.
- The avatar and icons are decorative (alt="" / aria-hidden).
- Touch targets of at least 44 × 44px.

## Reference implementation

Standalone HTML/CSS, tested in Chrome, Safari and Firefox:

\`\`\`html
<!-- Stampit badge · edit: https://stampit.example/create#c=abc -->
<style>.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-fast:linear(0,.08,.24,.409,.558,.678,.77,.838,.887,.922,.947,.964,.976,.984,.989,.993,.995,.997,.998,.999,1);--sp-test1234-attention:cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);--sp-test1234-repeat:linear}.sp-test1234,.sp-test1234 *,.sp-test1234 *::before,.sp-test1234 *::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0;border:0;font:inherit;line-height:inherit;letter-spacing:normal;text-transform:none;text-decoration:none;list-style:none;background:none;color:inherit;max-width:none;min-width:0;float:none}.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-bg:#ffffff;--sp-test1234-bd:#0000000d;--sp-test1234-tn:#6e6e73;--sp-test1234-tb:#000000;--sp-test1234-ic:#6e6e73;--sp-test1234-sh:rgba(0,0,0,.12);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;position:relative;vertical-align:middle;font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;line-height:1.2;text-align:left;white-space:nowrap;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale}.sp-test1234__pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;height:36px;padding:0 12px 0 4px;border-radius:18px;background:var(--sp-test1234-bg);box-shadow:0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.08);color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);white-space:nowrap;cursor:pointer;user-select:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;outline:none;transition:box-shadow .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast),transform .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast)}.sp-test1234__pill:hover{box-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.12)}@keyframes sp-test1234-in{0%,100%{transform:none}20%,60%{transform:translateX(-3px)}40%,80%{transform:translateX(3px)}}@keyframes sp-test1234-rp{0%{transform:translateX(-110%)}18%,100%{transform:translateX(110%)}}.sp-test1234{animation:sp-test1234-in .48s var(--sp-test1234-attention) backwards}.sp-test1234__pill{position:relative;overflow:hidden}.sp-test1234__pill::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;border-radius:inherit;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(105deg,transparent 30%,var(--sp-test1234-sh) 50%,transparent 70%);transform:translateX(110%);animation:sp-test1234-rp 5s var(--sp-test1234-repeat) 5s infinite}.sp-test1234__pill:hover{transform:scale(1.04)}.sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sp-test1234-tb);outline-offset:2px}.sp-test1234__av{flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;overflow:hidden;background:#ff6b35;color:#000000;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;line-height:1}.sp-test1234__n{color:var(--sp-test1234-tn)}.sp-test1234__b{color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);font-weight:500}.sp-test1234__ic{flex:none;display:block;color:var(--sp-test1234-ic);transition:transform .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast)}.sp-test1234__pill:hover .sp-test1234__ic,.sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible .sp-test1234__ic{transform:translate(2px,-2px)}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-bg:#14141c;--sp-test1234-bd:#2e2e3a;--sp-test1234-tn:#8a8a99;--sp-test1234-tb:#ffffff;--sp-test1234-ic:#8a8a99;--sp-test1234-sh:rgba(255,255,255,.55)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.sp-test1234__ic{transition:none}.sp-test1234,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:hover{animation:none;transform:none}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill::after{animation:none;opacity:0}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:hover .sp-test1234__ic,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible .sp-test1234__ic{transform:none}}</style>
<div class="sp-test1234">
  <a class="sp-test1234__pill" href="https://ada.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Crafted by Ada Lovelace, opens in a new tab">
    <span class="sp-test1234__av" aria-hidden="true">AL</span>
    <span><span class="sp-test1234__n">Crafted by</span> <span class="sp-test1234__b">Ada Lovelace</span></span>
    <svg class="sp-test1234__ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="7" y1="17" x2="17" y2="7"/><polyline points="7 7 17 7 17 17"/></svg>
  </a>
</div>
\`\`\`

