\`\`\`

## Acceptance criteria

1. Rendering: the page shows the badge at 36px high with the exact colors, radius, border and shadow above, in both light and dark site themes.
2. Hover: the arrow slides 2px up-right and the shadow grows, with no layout shift.
3. Click: the badge opens https://ada.dev in a new tab.
4. Keyboard: Tab reaches the badge, the focus ring is visible, Enter follows the link.
5. Reduced motion: with prefers-reduced-motion enabled, nothing moves; changes are instant or fades.
"
`;

exports[`generatePrompt > snapshot: profile-full 1`] = `
"# Add a "Made by" signature badge to this project

## Goal

Add this signature badge to the current project where the user wants it (in the footer if they haven't said where), using the project's own stack and conventions (components, styling approach, file structure). The badge reads "Launched by Olivier Tousche".
Match the visual spec and behavior below exactly. The reference implementation at the end is the source of truth: adapt it to the project rather than pasting it as-is when a native approach fits better. Add no new dependency.

## Visual spec

- Layout: Pill. [avatar] · normal text · bold text · icon, in one row, vertically centered, no wrapping.
- Order: normal text, then bold text. One regular space between them.
- Normal text: "Launched by", weight 400.
- Bold text: "Olivier Tousche", weight 500.
- Font: system stack only, no web font: -apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif.
- Size M: height 36px, font size 15px, padding 0 12px 0 4px, gap 8px.
- Corner radius: 18px (a full capsule).
- Border: none.
- Shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.08); on hover 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.12).
- Icon: an "arrow-up-right" (Lucide path: line 7,17 → 17,7 and polyline 7,7 17,7 17,17), 14px, 2px stroke, currentColor, in the icon color, aria-hidden (exact SVG in the reference).
- Avatar: round, 28px, image /olivier-avatar.png, object-fit: cover, background #FF6B35 behind transparent pixels. Decorative: alt="".
- Colors follow the site theme through prefers-color-scheme.
- Light palette:
  - Background: #FFFFFF
  - Border: #0000000D
  - Normal text: #6E6E73
  - Bold text: #000000
  - Icon: #6E6E73
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Dark palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Scope every class with a unique prefix and reset box-sizing, margin, padding, font, line-height and list-style on the badge and its children, so the host page CSS cannot leak in.

## Behavior

- Motion uses springs, expressed in CSS as linear() easings (values in the reference): fast = 0.08s, no bounce; moderate = 0.16s, no bounce; slow = 0.24s, bounce 0.12; slow exit = 0.16s tween. Never hard-code other durations.
- Mode: Profile. The badge is a button; clicking it opens a modal profile card. Hovering does nothing more than the hover effect.
- Modal: a native <dialog>, 400px wide (at most the viewport minus 32px), centered, 24px padding; on screens up to 480px wide, a full-width sheet docked to the bottom edge (top corners rounded, max 88dvh, safe-area padding at the bottom), rising 24px as it opens; scrolls inside when taller than the viewport. Same background, bold/normal text colors, border ring and font as the badge, corner radius 12 + 12 × the badge's roundness (px), shadow 0 24px 64px rgba(0,0,0,.24). Backdrop rgba(0,0,0,.4). The page does not scroll behind it.
- Opening: fade in and rise from translateY(8px) scale(.97) (slow spring, @starting-style); closing: the reverse (slow exit). Reduced motion: fade only.
- Close: a 32px round "×" button in the top-right corner (a <form method="dialog"> so it works without JS), Escape, or a click on the backdrop.
- Head: a 56px avatar (initials when there is no photo), then the name "Olivier Tousche" (18px, as an <h2>) and the role "Product designer" under it in the normal text color.
- Links row (wraps), links open in a new tab:
  - "Portfolio" https://olivier.dev: a 36px capsule filled with the bold text color, its text black or white (whichever reads), with a small up-right arrow.
  - GitHub https://github.com/olivier: a 36px round icon button, a faint tint of the bold text color with a 1px border ring, the logo in the icon color.
  - LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/in/olivier: a 36px round icon button, a faint tint of the bold text color with a 1px border ring, the logo in the icon color.
- "GitHub activity" section for @olivier: fetch https://api.github.com/users/olivier/events/public?per_page=100 (up to 3 pages, only while the 12-week window is not covered) the first time the modal opens, cache it in sessionStorage for 30 minutes. Draw only the bricks: one per day for the last 12 weeks plus the current one, 13 Sunday-first columns spanning the modal's width (square cells, 3px gaps), tinted with the bold text color by daily count (0, 1, 2–3, 4–6, 7+). No numbers or labels: the grid is one link to the GitHub profile, named "GitHub profile of @olivier: N public events in the last 12 weeks". A pulsing placeholder while loading; on error, hide the section.
- "Projects" section, a list of cards (faint tint of the bold text color, 1px border ring), each with the name and a short description in the normal text color, the whole card a link with an up-right arrow:
  1. Stampit — https://stampit.app — "Signature badges for side projects"
- Section titles: 12px, upper-case, letter-spacing .04em, normal text color.
- Hover and keyboard focus: the arrow slides 2px up and 2px right (fast spring).
- Hover: the shadow grows as specified (fast spring).
- On appear: the badge gives a short horizontal shake (±3px). Animate a wrapper, not the clickable element, so the hover effect never restarts it.
- On delay: every 5s, starting 5s after load, the badge shows a sheen sweeping once from left to right across it (a gradient band on a clipped ::after: white on dark surfaces, a faint dark band on light ones). Loop it with CSS (one keyframe cycle per period), no timers.
- On hover: the badge scales to 1.04 (fast spring).
- prefers-reduced-motion: reduce → no movement, rotation or scaling; state changes are instant or fade only.

## Accessibility

- The badge is a <button type="button"> named "Launched by Olivier Tousche, open profile", with aria-haspopup="dialog" and aria-controls pointing at the dialog.
- The modal is a native <dialog> opened with showModal(): focus moves into it and stays there, Escape closes it, and focus returns to the badge. It is labelled by the name heading.
- The close button is named "Close". Links that open in a new tab say so in their name.
- Visible focus: a 2px outline in the bold text color, offset 2px, on :focus-visible.
- The avatar and icons are decorative (alt="" / aria-hidden).
- Touch targets of at least 44 × 44px.

## Reference implementation

Standalone HTML/CSS/JS, tested in Chrome, Safari and Firefox:

\`\`\`html
